      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I can certainly make the tone warmer and more human, but I must warn you that even a \"human\" email from a luxury brand needs to be careful not to sound *too* casual, as that might undermine the exclusivity you're trying to maintain. However, I will infuse the draft with a bit more warmth and acknowledge the chaotic nature of logistics while keeping the high-end feel.\n\n***\n\n**Subject:** A Heartfelt Note About Your Order & How We're Fixing It\n\nHi [Customer Name],\n\nI wanted to reach out personally because I know how frustrating it is to wait for something so special, especially when it's past the date you were hoping to receive it. I can feel your disappointment, and I want to say how sorry I am that your order is currently stuck at our Memphis hub.\n\nSometimes, even in the most carefully planned logistics chains, the world throws us unexpected curveballs—like a sudden traffic jam, a weather delay, or just a very stubborn sorting system that refuses to cooperate. While we can't control every variable in the supply chain, we are on it. Our team is working overtime to get your package moving again, and I promise you that we are prioritizing your delivery above everything",
